{"pattern_name": "Unsafe Dynamic Property Access", "functionality": "The code dynamically accesses and manipulates properties on an object using user-controlled input, enforcing a naming convention and reserved property check.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code dynamically constructs property access strings (e.g., `this['${reservedProperty}']['${prop}']`) based on user-controlled input (`prop`). If `prop` is not properly sanitized, an attacker could inject malicious property names or values, leading to unintended behavior or security vulnerabilities.", "vulnerable_example": "const setter = new Function('value', `this['${reservedProperty}']['${prop}'] = value;`);\nconst getter = new Function(`return this['${reservedProperty}']['${prop}'];`);", "fixing_pattern": "To fix this vulnerability, avoid dynamically constructing property access strings. Instead, use explicit property access or validate and sanitize the input (`prop`) to ensure it adheres to the expected format and does not contain malicious content.", "fixing_example": "const setter = function(value) {\n    if (prop.startsWith(reservedPrefix) && obj.hasOwnProperty(reservedProperty)) {\n        obj[reservedProperty][prop] = value;\n    }\n};\nconst getter = function() {\n    if (prop.startsWith(reservedPrefix) && obj.hasOwnProperty(reservedProperty)) {\n        return obj[reservedProperty][prop];\n    }\n};"}
