{"pattern_name": "Hardcoded Credentials in Test Code", "functionality": "The code tests login functionality by simulating user interactions with a web form, submitting incorrect credentials, and verifying the response message.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code uses hardcoded passwords ('wrongpassword' and 'anypassword') in test cases, which is an unsafe practice. Hardcoded credentials can lead to security risks if the test code is deployed or exposed, as attackers can exploit these credentials.", "vulnerable_example": "def test_login_with_incorrect_password(testapp, user):\n    res = testapp.get('/')\n    form = res.forms['loginForm']\n    form['email'] = user.email\n    form['password'] = 'testpassword123'\n    res = form.submit()\n    assert 'Invalid login credentials' in res.text", "fixing_pattern": "Replace hardcoded credentials with dynamically generated or securely managed credentials. Use environment variables or a secret management system to store and retrieve test credentials securely.", "fixing_example": "import os\n\ndef test_login_with_incorrect_password(testapp, user):\n    res = testapp.get('/')\n    form = res.forms['loginForm']\n    form['email'] = user.email\n    form['password'] = os.getenv('TEST_INCORRECT_PASSWORD')\n    res = form.submit()\n    assert 'Invalid login credentials' in res.text"}
