{"pattern_name": "Unnecessary Resource Initialization on Connection", "functionality": "The code initializes backend plugins and prepares them for each new connection, even if the connection might not proceed to the actual request processing phase.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code performs backend initialization (`backend_open` and `backend_prepare`) immediately after establishing a connection, regardless of whether the connection will be used for actual requests.", "vulnerable_example": "lock_request (conn);\nr = backend_open (backend, conn, read_only);\nunlock_request (conn);\nif (r == -1)\n  goto done;\nlock_request (conn);\nif (backend)\n  r = backend_prepare (backend, conn);\nelse\n  r = 0;\nunlock_request (conn);\nif (r == -1)\n  goto done;", "fixing_pattern": "The fix removes the unnecessary backend initialization (`backend_open` and `backend_prepare`) steps during the connection phase, deferring them until they are actually needed for processing requests.", "fixing_example": ""}
{"pattern_name": "Missing CSRF Protection in HTTP PUT Method", "functionality": "The code defines a generic controller that handles HTTP requests for a given model type. It includes methods for retrieving, adding, and updating model instances using a repository interface.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The `[HttpPut]` method handler lacks the `[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]` attribute, which is necessary to protect against Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks. Without this attribute, the application cannot verify that the request originated from an authorized user, making it vulnerable to unauthorized state-changing requests.", "vulnerable_example": "[HttpPut(\"{id}\")]\npublic ActionResult Put(int id, [FromBody] T updatedModel)\n{\n    if (updatedModel == null)\n    {\n        return BadRequest();\n    }\n\n    var existingModel = repository.Get(id);\n    if (existingModel == null)\n    {\n        return NotFound();\n    }\n\n    var allowedFields = new[] { \"Text\", \"Done\", \"Order\" };\n    UpdateModel(existingModel, allowedFields);\n\n    if (!TryValidateModel(existingModel))\n    {\n        return BadRequest(ModelState);\n    }\n\n    repository.Update(existingModel);\n    return NoContent();\n}", "fixing_pattern": "To resolve the vulnerability, the `[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]` attribute should be added to the `[HttpPut]` method. This ensures that the application validates the anti-forgery token included in the request, confirming that the request is legitimate and originated from an authorized user.", "fixing_example": "[HttpPut(\"{id}\")]\n[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]\npublic ActionResult Put(int id, [FromBody] T updatedModel)\n{\n    if (updatedModel == null)\n    {\n        return BadRequest();\n    }\n\n    var existingModel = repository.Get(id);\n    if (existingModel == null)\n    {\n        return NotFound();\n    }\n\n    var allowedFields = new[] { \"Text\", \"Done\", \"Order\" };\n    UpdateModel(existingModel, allowedFields);\n\n    if (!TryValidateModel(existingModel))\n    {\n        return BadRequest(ModelState);\n    }\n\n    repository.Update(existingModel);\n    return NoContent();\n}"}
