{"pattern_name": "Missing NULL Pointer Validation Before Dereference", "functionality": "The code processes an assignment expression and performs operations on the left-hand side (lhs) variable without validating if it is NULL.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Performing operations on a potentially NULL pointer without validation, which can lead to NULL pointer dereference.", "vulnerable_example": "if (JSP_SHOULD_EXECUTE) {\n  if (op=='=') {\n    jspReplaceWithOrAddToRoot(lhs, rhs);\n  } else {\n    // ... operations on lhs without NULL check\n  }\n}", "fixing_pattern": "Adding a NULL check before performing operations on the pointer to prevent dereferencing a NULL pointer.", "fixing_example": "if (JSP_SHOULD_EXECUTE && lhs) {\n  if (op=='=') {\n    jspReplaceWithOrAddToRoot(lhs, rhs);\n  } else {\n    // ... operations on lhs after NULL check\n  }\n}"}
