{"pattern_name": "Unescaped User Input in HTML Output", "functionality": "The code constructs an HTML response that includes user-controlled input directly in the HTML content without proper escaping.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Directly embedding user-controlled input into HTML output without escaping, which can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities.", "vulnerable_example": "sendReply(HttpResponseStatus.BAD_REQUEST,\n                makePage(\"Bad Request\", \"Looks like it's your fault this time\",\n                         \"<blockquote>\"\n                         + \"<h1>Bad Request</h1>\"\n                         + \"Sorry but your request was rejected as being\"\n                         + \" invalid.<br/><br/>\"\n                         + \"The reason provided was:<blockquote>\"\n                         + exception.getMessage()\n                         + \"</blockquote></blockquote>\"));", "fixing_pattern": "Escaping user-controlled input before embedding it into HTML output to prevent XSS vulnerabilities.", "fixing_example": "String response = \"\";\n      if (exception.getMessage() != null) {\n        response = HtmlEscapers.htmlEscaper().escape(exception.getMessage());\n      }\n      sendReply(HttpResponseStatus.BAD_REQUEST,\n                makePage(\"Bad Request\", \"Looks like it's your fault this time\",\n                         \"<blockquote>\"\n                         + \"<h1>Bad Request</h1>\"\n                         + \"Sorry but your request was rejected as being\"\n                         + \" invalid.<br/><br/>\"\n                         + \"The reason provided was:<blockquote>\"\n                         + response\n                         + \"</blockquote></blockquote>\"));"}
