{"pattern_name": "Hardcoded API Key", "functionality": "The code processes a route request by validating user input, constructing a URL with coordinates and waypoints, and querying the Google Maps Directions API to retrieve route data.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The API key is hardcoded directly in the source code, making it easily accessible to anyone with access to the codebase. This exposes the key to potential misuse, especially if the code is shared or leaked.", "vulnerable_example": "<?php\n$apikey = 'AIzaSyB9_vfqgqGrIwOeY3tN9tHztRVEU_J7JwM';\n// Rest of the code...\n?>", "fixing_pattern": "The API key should be stored in a secure environment variable or configuration file outside the codebase. This ensures the key is not exposed in the source code and can be managed securely.", "fixing_example": "<?php\n$apikey = getenv('GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY');\n// Rest of the code...\n?>"}
{"pattern_name": "Unsafe Path Concatenation", "functionality": "Concatenates a path and a filename without proper validation of the filename.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code concatenates a path and a filename without validating the filename for unsafe characters or sequences, which can lead to invalid memory access or path traversal vulnerabilities.", "vulnerable_example": "char *concat_path_basename(const char *path, const char *filename)\n{\n    char *abspath = realpath(filename, NULL);\n    char *base = strrchr((abspath ? abspath : filename), '/');\n    char buf[sizeof(\"tmp-\"LIBREPORT_ISO_DATE_STRING_SAMPLE\"-%lu\")];\n    if (base && base[1] != '\\0' && base[1] != '.')\n    {\n        base++;\n    }\n    else\n    {\n        sprintf(buf, \"tmp-%s-%lu\", iso_date_string(NULL), (long)getpid());\n        base = buf;\n    }\n    char *name = concat_path_file(path, base);\n    free(abspath);\n    return name;\n}", "fixing_pattern": "The fix introduces a function to validate the filename for unsafe characters and sequences before processing it. This ensures that only safe filenames are used in path concatenation.", "fixing_example": "bool str_is_correct_filename(const char *str)\n{\n#define NOT_PRINTABLE(c) (c < ' ' || c == 0x7f)\n    if (NOT_PRINTABLE(*str) || *str == '/' || *str == '\\0')\n        return false;\n    ++str;\n    if (NOT_PRINTABLE(*str) || *str =='/' || (*str == '\\0' && *(str-1) == '.'))\n        return false;\n    ++str;\n    if (NOT_PRINTABLE(*str) || *str =='/' || (*str == '\\0' && *(str-1) == '.' && *(str-2) == '.'))\n        return false;\n    ++str;\n    for (unsigned i = 0; *str != '\\0' && i < 61; ++str, ++i)\n        if (NOT_PRINTABLE(*str) || *str == '/')\n            return false;\n    return *str == '\\0';\n#undef NOT_PRINTABLE\n}"}
{"pattern_name": "Missing Control Object Validation", "functionality": "The code attempts to create and use control objects without verifying their successful creation.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Using control objects without checking if they were successfully created.", "vulnerable_example": "ControlObjectClient control = ControlObjectClient_create(\"simpleIOGenericIO/GGIO1.SPCSO1\", con);\n// Immediately using 'control' without checking if it's valid", "fixing_pattern": "Adding validation checks to ensure control objects are successfully created before using them.", "fixing_example": "ControlObjectClient control = ControlObjectClient_create(\"simpleIOGenericIO/GGIO1.SPCSO1\", con);\nif (control) {\n    // Safe to use 'control'\n}"}
{"pattern_name": "Incomplete File Upload Error Handling", "functionality": "The code processes file uploads from HTTP requests and handles potential errors during parsing.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code only catches MultiPartParserError when handling file uploads, potentially missing other critical file-related errors that could be exploited.", "vulnerable_example": "try:\n    self._post, self._files = self.parse_file_upload(self.META, data)\nexcept MultiPartParserError:\n    self._mark_post_parse_error()\n    raise", "fixing_pattern": "The fix adds additional error handling by catching TooManyFilesSent exception along with MultiPartParserError, providing more comprehensive protection against file upload-related vulnerabilities.", "fixing_example": "try:\n    self._post, self._files = self.parse_file_upload(self.META, data)\nexcept (MultiPartParserError, TooManyFilesSent):\n    self._mark_post_parse_error()\n    raise"}
{"pattern_name": "Unsafe File Concatenation", "functionality": "The code concatenates the contents of multiple files into a single output file.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code does not validate the file paths before reading and concatenating their contents, which could allow an attacker to include unintended files in the output.", "vulnerable_example": "const contents = filePaths.map(filePath => fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8'));\nfs.writeFileSync(outputFilePath, contents.join('\n'));", "fixing_pattern": "Validate and sanitize all file paths before reading and concatenating their contents. Use a whitelist of allowed files and ensure that the final output file is within an intended directory.", "fixing_example": "const allowedFiles = ['/safe/file1.txt', '/safe/file2.txt'];\nif (!filePaths.every(filePath => allowedFiles.includes(filePath))) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid file path');\n}\nconst contents = filePaths.map(filePath => fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8'));\nfs.writeFileSync(outputFilePath, contents.join('\n'));"}
{"pattern_name": "Unvalidated Function Return Value", "functionality": "The code calls functions to create a digest response but does not check the return value for errors.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The functions `pjsip_auth_create_digest` and `pjsip_auth_create_digestSHA256` are called without checking their return values, which could lead to undefined behavior if they fail.", "vulnerable_example": "pjsip_auth_create_digest(&cred->response, &cred->nonce, NULL, NULL, NULL, uri, &chal->realm, cred_info, method);", "fixing_pattern": "The fix involves capturing the return value of these functions and returning it to ensure any errors are properly handled.", "fixing_example": "status = pjsip_auth_create_digest(&cred->response, &cred->nonce, NULL, NULL, NULL, uri, &chal->realm, cred_info, method);\nreturn status;"}
