{"pattern_name": "Unsafe Context Object Usage", "functionality": "The code uses a context object (h2_ctx) to retrieve server configuration settings, which can lead to misconfiguration if the context is not properly initialized or synchronized.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Using a context object (h2_ctx) to retrieve server configuration settings, which can lead to misconfiguration if the context is not properly initialized or synchronized.", "vulnerable_example": "session->s = h2_ctx_server_get(ctx);\nsession->config = h2_config_sget(session->s);\nsession->max_stream_count = h2_config_geti(session->config, H2_CONF_MAX_STREAMS);", "fixing_pattern": "Directly passing the server configuration settings as a parameter to the function, ensuring that the configuration is consistent and properly initialized.", "fixing_example": "session->s = s;\nsession->max_stream_count = h2_config_sgeti(s, H2_CONF_MAX_STREAMS);"}
{"pattern_name": "Overly Complex Setup with Potential Security Risks", "functionality": "The code sets up a complex environment for testing, including mock objects and configurations for various components like identity, certificates, and DBus interfaces.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The setup method initializes multiple components and mocks, including DBus interfaces, without clear access control mechanisms. This complexity can lead to unintended exposure of sensitive methods or data.", "vulnerable_example": "def setUp(self):\n    self.addCleanup(patch.stopall)\n    cfg_patcher = patch.object(subscription_manager.managercli, 'cfg', new=stubs.config.CFG)\n    self.mock_cfg = cfg_patcher.start()\n    id_mock = NonCallableMock(name='FixtureIdentityMock')\n    id_mock.exists_and_valid = Mock(return_value=True)\n    id_mock.uuid = 'fixture_identity_mock_uuid'\n    id_mock.name = 'fixture_identity_mock_name'\n    id_mock.cert_dir_path = \"/not/a/real/path/to/pki/consumer/\"\n    id_mock.keypath.return_value = \"/not/a/real/key/path\"\n    id_mock.certpath.return_value = \"/not/a/real/cert/path\"\n    self.mock_calc = NonCallableMock()\n    self.mock_calc.calculate.return_value = None\n    self.mock_repofile_path_exists_patcher = patch('subscription_manager.repolib.RepoFile.path_exists')\n    mock_repofile_path_exists = self.mock_repofile_path_exists_patcher.start()\n    mock_repofile_path_exists.return_value = True\n    inj.provide(inj.IDENTITY, id_mock)\n    inj.provide(inj.PRODUCT_DATE_RANGE_CALCULATOR, self.mock_calc)\n    inj.provide(inj.ENTITLEMENT_STATUS_CACHE, stubs.StubEntitlementStatusCache())\n    inj.provide(inj.PROD_STATUS_CACHE, stubs.StubProductStatusCache())\n    inj.provide(inj.OVERRIDE_STATUS_CACHE, stubs.StubOverrideStatusCache())\n    inj.provide(inj.RELEASE_STATUS_CACHE, stubs.StubReleaseStatusCache())\n    inj.provide(inj.PROFILE_MANAGER, stubs.StubProfileManager())\n    self.ent_dir = stubs.StubEntitlementDirectory()\n    inj.provide(inj.ENT_DIR, self.ent_dir)\n    self.prod_dir = stubs.StubProductDirectory()\n    inj.provide(inj.PROD_DIR, self.prod_dir)\n    inj.provide(inj.INSTALLED_PRODUCTS_MANAGER, stubs.StubInstalledProductsManager())\n    self.stub_cp_provider = stubs.StubCPProvider()\n    self._release_versions = []\n    self.stub_cp_provider.content_connection.get_versions = self._get_release_versions\n    inj.provide(inj.CP_PROVIDER, self.stub_cp_provider)\n    inj.provide(inj.CERT_SORTER, stubs.StubCertSorter())\n    plugin_manager_mock = MagicMock(name='FixturePluginManagerMock')\n    plugin_manager_mock.runiter.return_value = iter([])\n    inj.provide(inj.PLUGIN_MANAGER, plugin_manager_mock)\n    inj.provide(inj.DBUS_IFACE, Mock(name='FixtureDbusIfaceMock'))\n    pooltype_cache = Mock()\n    inj.provide(inj.POOLTYPE_CACHE, pooltype_cache)\n    inj.provide(inj.ACTION_LOCK, RLock)\n    self.stub_facts = stubs.StubFacts()\n    inj.provide(inj.FACTS, self.stub_facts)\n    self.dbus_patcher = patch('subscription_manager.managercli.CliCommand._request_validity_check')\n    self.dbus_patcher.start()\n    self.is_valid_server_patcher = patch(\"subscription_manager.managercli.is_valid_server_info\")\n    is_valid_server_mock = self.is_valid_server_patcher.start()\n    is_valid_server_mock.return_value = True\n    self.test_proxy_connection_patcher = patch(\"subscription_manager.managercli.CliCommand.test_proxy_connection\")\n    test_proxy_connection_mock = self.test_proxy_connection_patcher.start()\n    test_proxy_connection_mock.return_value = True\n    self.files_to_cleanup = []", "fixing_pattern": "The fix simplifies the setup by removing the complex initialization of multiple components and mocks, reducing the attack surface and potential security risks.", "fixing_example": "def set_facts(self):\n    return {\"mock.facts\": \"true\"}"}
{"pattern_name": "Unnecessary Parameter Exposure", "functionality": "The method runs tests by setting properties, enqueuing content, and asserting flow file attributes. It previously allowed for the configuration of validation skipping and pretty printing through parameters.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Exposing parameters that control validation and output formatting can lead to unintended bypassing of security checks or exposure of sensitive information.", "vulnerable_example": "private void runTests(final String content, Map<String, String> expectedAttributes, final boolean skipValidation, final boolean prettyPrinting) throws IOException {", "fixing_pattern": "Removing unnecessary parameters that could be used to bypass validation or expose sensitive information. Hardcoding the validation skip to true ensures that the method always skips validation, reducing the attack surface.", "fixing_example": "private void runTests(final String content, final Map<String, String> expectedAttributes) {"}
{"pattern_name": "Incomplete Access Control for API Endpoints", "functionality": "The code generates links to API endpoints without ensuring that the user has the necessary permissions to access those endpoints.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code generates links to API endpoints (e.g., for inserting or dropping tables) without verifying if the user has the required permissions.", "vulnerable_example": "table_links.append({'path': self.ds.urls.table(name, table) + '/-/drop', 'label': 'Drop table ' + table, 'json': {'confirm': False}, 'method': 'POST'})", "fixing_pattern": "The code now explicitly checks if the user has the necessary permissions (e.g., 'insert-row', 'drop-table') before generating links to sensitive API endpoints.", "fixing_example": "if await self.ds.permission_allowed(request.actor, 'drop-table', (name, table)): table_links.append({'path': self.ds.urls.table(name, table) + '/-/drop', 'label': 'Drop table ' + table, 'json': {'confirm': False}, 'method': 'POST'})"}
{"pattern_name": "Hardcoded Credentials in Configuration", "functionality": "The code retrieves database configuration settings based on the environment (CI or default). It dynamically selects the database, user, and password based on whether the CI environment variable is set to 'true'.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code hardcodes sensitive credentials (passwords) directly in the source code. This is a common insecure practice that exposes credentials to anyone with access to the codebase, making it easier for attackers to exploit.", "vulnerable_example": "def get_database_config():\n    if os.environ.get('CI') == 'true':\n        password = 'ci_password'\n    else:\n        password = 'default_password'\n    return {'password': password}", "fixing_pattern": "To resolve this vulnerability, sensitive credentials should be stored securely using a secret management system (e.g., environment variables, vaults, or cloud-based secret managers). The code should retrieve credentials from these secure sources instead of hardcoding them.", "fixing_example": "def get_database_config():\n    password = os.environ.get('DB_PASSWORD', 'fallback_password')\n    return {'password': password}"}
{"pattern_name": "Missing Authorization in Database Operations", "functionality": "The code connects to a SQLite database, creates a table with specified columns and a primary key, and queries the database based on provided conditions. It returns the results of the query.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code lacks proper authorization checks before executing critical database operations, such as creating a table or querying data. This allows unauthorized users to perform potentially harmful actions on the database.", "vulnerable_example": "<?php\nfunction createAndQueryTable($dbname, $table, $columns, $primaryKey, $conditions) {\n    $db = new PDO(\"sqlite:$dbname\");\n    $db->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);\n    $columnDefinitions = implode(\", \", $columns);\n    $sql = \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS $table ($columnDefinitions, PRIMARY KEY ($primaryKey))\";\n    $db->exec($sql); // Vulnerable line\n    $query = \"SELECT * FROM $table WHERE $conditions\";\n    $stmt = $db->prepare($query);\n    $stmt->execute();\n    return $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);\n}\n?>", "fixing_pattern": "Implement authorization checks to ensure that only authorized users can perform critical database operations. This can be done by validating user permissions before executing the database query or table creation.", "fixing_example": "<?php\nfunction createAndQueryTable($dbname, $table, $columns, $primaryKey, $conditions, $userRole) {\n    if ($userRole !== 'admin') {\n        throw new Exception(\"Unauthorized access\");\n    }\n    $db = new PDO(\"sqlite:$dbname\");\n    $db->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);\n    $columnDefinitions = implode(\", \", $columns);\n    $sql = \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS $table ($columnDefinitions, PRIMARY KEY ($primaryKey))\";\n    $db->exec($sql); // Now protected by authorization check\n    $query = \"SELECT * FROM $table WHERE $conditions\";\n    $stmt = $db->prepare($query);\n    $stmt->execute();\n    return $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);\n}\n?>"}
{"pattern_name": "Insufficient Sibling Validation", "functionality": "The code attempts to add a route to a node in the routing table, checking if the route has siblings.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code does not validate if the sibling route qualifies for ECMP before adding it to the sibling list, potentially leading to incorrect routing behavior.", "vulnerable_example": "if (sibling->rt6i_metric == rt->rt6i_metric) {\n    list_add_tail(&rt->rt6i_siblings,\n                  &sibling->rt6i_siblings);\n    break;\n}", "fixing_pattern": "The fix introduces a validation function `rt6_qualify_for_ecmp` to ensure that the sibling route qualifies for ECMP before adding it to the sibling list.", "fixing_example": "if (sibling->rt6i_metric == rt->rt6i_metric &&\n    rt6_qualify_for_ecmp(sibling)) {\n    list_add_tail(&rt->rt6i_siblings,\n                  &sibling->rt6i_siblings);\n    break;\n}"}
{"pattern_name": "Unchecked String Concatenation", "functionality": "The function appends path components to a destination buffer without verifying if the buffer has enough space for the concatenated result.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code appends strings to the destination buffer and increments the pointer without checking if the destination buffer can accommodate the new data, risking buffer overflow.", "vulnerable_example": "p += udf_get_filename(sb, pc->componentIdent, p, pc->lengthComponentIdent);\n*p++ = '/';", "fixing_pattern": "The fix adds a length check (`tolen`) before appending data to the destination buffer. If the remaining space is insufficient, the function returns an error code (`-ENAMETOOLONG`).", "fixing_example": "comp_len = udf_get_filename(sb, pc->componentIdent, pc->lengthComponentIdent, p, tolen);\np += comp_len;\ntolen -= comp_len;\nif (tolen == 0)\n    return -ENAMETOOLONG;\n*p++ = '/';\ntolen--;"}
{"pattern_name": "Unencoded URI Path", "functionality": "The code processes a request URI to determine the action to be taken but does not encode the URI path, which can lead to security vulnerabilities.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The request URI is used directly without encoding, which can allow for injection attacks or misinterpretation of the URI.", "vulnerable_example": "String requestUri = getRequestContext().getRequestUri();", "fixing_pattern": "The request URI is encoded using the specified character encoding to ensure that it is properly formatted and secure.", "fixing_example": "String requestUri = getRequestContext().getRequestUri();\nString encoding = pageContext.getResponse().getCharacterEncoding();\ntry {\n    requestUri = UriUtils.encodePath(requestUri, encoding);\n} catch (UnsupportedEncodingException e) {\n    throw new JspException(e);\n}"}
{"pattern_name": "Insecure Path Construction", "functionality": "The code constructs a file path by concatenating a base directory with a user-controlled filename.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Using string concatenation to construct file paths can lead to path traversal or symlink attacks if the input is not properly sanitized.", "vulnerable_example": "npath = self.data + '/' + notifier", "fixing_pattern": "Using `os.path.join()` to safely construct file paths, which handles path separators correctly and reduces the risk of path manipulation.", "fixing_example": "npath = os.path.join(self.data, notifier)"}
{"pattern_name": "Insecure Temporary File Path Handling", "functionality": "The code processes file uploads and handles temporary file paths, including sanitizing file names to ensure they are safe for use in the filesystem.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code does not properly handle spaces in temporary file paths, which can lead to misinterpretation of the path and unintended file operations (e.g., deletion).", "vulnerable_example": "file_name = force_text(file_name, encoding, errors='replace')\nfile_name = self.sanitize_file_name(file_name)", "fixing_pattern": "The fix ensures that spaces in temporary file paths are properly handled by adding additional checks and safeguards to prevent misinterpretation of the path.", "fixing_example": "file_name = force_text(file_name, encoding, errors='replace')\nfile_name = self.sanitize_file_name(file_name)\n# Additional checks and safeguards are added to handle spaces in paths"}
{"pattern_name": "Unrestricted File Upload Without Validation", "functionality": "The code processes file uploads by retrieving file paths from a request and directly fetching the files from storage without validating the file type or origin.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code accepts file paths from user input and directly fetches the files from storage without any validation or verification of the file's safety or origin.", "vulnerable_example": "request.FILES.setlist(field_name, list(self.get_files_from_storage(paths)))", "fixing_pattern": "The fix introduces validation by requiring a signature for the file upload and checking for suspicious file operations. This ensures that only authorized and safe files are processed.", "fixing_example": "request.FILES.setlist(field_name, list(self.get_files_from_storage(paths, signature)))"}
