{"pattern_name": "Hardcoded Template Paths", "functionality": "The code defines Django views for handling password reset functionality, including confirmation and completion. It uses hardcoded template paths to render the appropriate HTML pages for these views.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code directly hardcodes the paths to the template files within the class definitions. This practice is insecure because it embeds configuration details directly in the code, making it difficult to change without modifying the source and potentially exposing sensitive paths.", "vulnerable_example": "class ResetPasswordConfirmView(BaseAdminView):\n    password_reset_confirm_template = 'xadmin/auth/password_reset/confirm.html'\n\nclass ResetPasswordCompleteView(BaseAdminView):\n    password_reset_complete_template = 'xadmin/auth/password_reset/complete.html'", "fixing_pattern": "To resolve this issue, the template paths should be moved to a configuration file or environment variables. This allows for easier management and updates without modifying the source code, enhancing security and flexibility.", "fixing_example": "from django.conf import settings\n\nclass ResetPasswordConfirmView(BaseAdminView):\n    password_reset_confirm_template = settings.PASSWORD_RESET_CONFIRM_TEMPLATE\n\nclass ResetPasswordCompleteView(BaseAdminView):\n    password_reset_complete_template = settings.PASSWORD_RESET_COMPLETE_TEMPLATE"}
{"pattern_name": "Insecure JWT Token Validation", "functionality": "The system processes authentication requests using JWT tokens without proper validation of the token's signature or claims.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Accepting and processing JWT tokens without verifying their authenticity or integrity.", "vulnerable_example": "// Hypothetical example\npublic void handleLogin(JWT token) {\n    String username = token.getClaim(\"username\");\n    authenticateUser(username);\n}", "fixing_pattern": "Implement proper JWT validation including signature verification and claim validation.", "fixing_example": "// Hypothetical example\npublic void handleLogin(JWT token) {\n    if (!verifySignature(token)) {\n        throw new SecurityException(\"Invalid token\");\n    }\n    if (!validateClaims(token)) {\n        throw new SecurityException(\"Invalid claims\");\n    }\n    String username = token.getClaim(\"username\");\n    authenticateUser(username);\n}"}
