{"pattern_name": "Incomplete Event Unsubscription", "functionality": "The code is responsible for unsubscribing from various events when the plugin is stopped. This ensures that the plugin does not continue to receive or process events after it has been deactivated.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code fails to unsubscribe from all relevant events, leaving some event handlers still active after the plugin is stopped. This can lead to unintended behavior or resource leaks.", "vulnerable_example": "def stop(self):\n    self.bus.log('Stop Notification plugin')\n    self.bus.publish('unschedule_job', self.notification_job)\n    self.bus.unsubscribe('access_token_added', self.access_token_added)\n    self.bus.unsubscribe('user_attr_changed', self.user_attr_changed)\n    self.bus.unsubscribe('user_password_changed', self.user_password_changed)", "fixing_pattern": "The fix involves adding the missing unsubscription for the 'authorizedkey_added' event, ensuring that all event handlers are properly unsubscribed when the plugin is stopped.", "fixing_example": "def stop(self):\n    self.bus.log('Stop Notification plugin')\n    self.bus.publish('unschedule_job', self.notification_job)\n    self.bus.unsubscribe('access_token_added', self.access_token_added)\n    self.bus.unsubscribe('authorizedkey_added', self.authorizedkey_added)\n    self.bus.unsubscribe('user_attr_changed', self.user_attr_changed)\n    self.bus.unsubscribe('user_password_changed', self.user_password_changed)"}
