{"pattern_name": "Incomplete Command-Line Argument Processing", "functionality": "The code processes command-line arguments to determine server operations but initially lacks handling for additional options.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code only checks for basic operations (start, stop, etc.) without properly parsing additional command-line options that might be needed for proper process management.", "vulnerable_example": "def process_command_line(self, argv, verbose=1):\n    usage = \"usage:  %s  start | stop | restart | status | debug \" \\\n                \"(run as non-daemon)\" % os.path.basename(argv[0])\n    if len(argv) < 2:\n        print usage\n        raise SystemExit\n    else:\n        operation = argv[1]", "fixing_pattern": "The code is enhanced to properly parse additional command-line options (specifically --pidfile) by checking for and extracting the value of the --pidfile option if present.", "fixing_example": "def process_command_line(self, argv, verbose=1):\n    usage = \"usage:  %s  start | stop | restart | status | debug \" \\\n                \"[--pidfile=...] \" \\\n                \"(run as non-daemon)\" % os.path.basename(argv[0])\n    if len(argv) < 2:\n        print usage\n        raise SystemExit\n    else:\n        operation = argv[1]\n        if len(argv) > 2 and argv[2].startswith('--pidfile=') and \\\n            len(argv[2]) > len('--pidfile='):\n            self.pidfile = argv[2][len('--pidfile='):]"}
